From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: a reload's SYN flood rate reaches every address

Each address in the SYN flood sets has its own limit, made at the rate in
force when the address was first seen. A reload flushes the table's rules
but not its sets' elements, so a lowered rate didn't reach an address the
set already had: it kept the old rate until it had been quiet for a minute,
and a flood from it never is. Empty the sets on every load, in the same
transaction as the new rules; addresses come back at the new rate on their
next SYN.

Signed-off-by: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
---
--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
@@ -483,7 +483,12 @@
 {% fw4.includes('chain-append', 'mangle_forward') %}
 	}
 {% fw4.includes('table-append') %}
 }
+{% if (fw4.default_option("synflood_protect") && fw4.default_option("synflood_rate")): %}
+
+flush set inet fw4 syn_flood_v4
+flush set inet fw4 syn_flood_v6
+{% endif %}
 {% if (bridge_offload): %}
 
 table bridge fw4
